@startuml
title EventEase - Activity Diagram (Attendance Request Approval)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 10
skinparam activityBorderColor Black
skinparam activityBackgroundColor White
skinparam ArrowColor Black

' This flow runs ONCE PER REQUEST, and a request is ONE missed lecture.
' That is why CC credits do not appear here: they are per (volunteer, event),
' awarded by the Team Head after the event. Assigning them on request approval
' would pay out five times for five lectures missed at one event.
'
' Report generation and teacher downloads are not here either — a teacher
' downloads whenever they like; it is not triggered by an approval. And nothing
' is "generated and stored": the CSV is built on the spot from a query.
'
' No "Notify Volunteer" step — notifications are future scope per the synopsis.
' The volunteer sees the status on their dashboard.

start

:Login;

:Create Attendance Request;

:Select Event;

:Select Subject;

:Enter Lecture Details;

:Enter Reason;

:Submit Request;

:Validate Request;

if (Duplicate Request?) then (Yes)

:Display Duplicate Request;

stop

else (No)

:Forward to Team Head;

endif

:Team Head Reviews Request;

if (Approved by Team Head?) then (No)

:Record Rejection and Remark;

:Status = Rejected;

stop

else (Yes)

:Record Approval, Time and Remark;

:Status = Pending President;

:Forward to President;

endif

:President Verifies Request;

if (Approved by President?) then (No)

:Record Rejection and Remark;

:Status = Rejected;

stop

else (Yes)

:Record Verification and Time;

:Status = Approved;

:Count Lecture on Class Attendance Sheet;

stop

endif

@enduml
